      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's completely understandable that those platitudes feel hollow when you're deep in this kind of exhaustion. The quiet you crave isn't a failure; it's a desperate need for the pain to finally stop. If the current structure of things feels unbearable, maybe the most immediate act of self-care is finding a way to make the *next* minute less agonizing. There are people who understand the depth of this specific kind of weariness, even if they can't fix the situation.",
